{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1136","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1136","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1136\",\"parent_revision\":\"4b9771bc9cf4945fd7d506cc562dd0f04e8a7783\",\"root_revision\":\"35865f7cc34177b816861e648f41a9cded9ae2588ca7d0637a6c626196f787fd\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nA standalone skill that batch-triages all open P0/P1 backlog items for staleness without executing any of them. Reads from local cache (422 files, 237 open P0+P1), cross-references against working tree and git log, and produces a triage report.\\n\\n**Algorithm (Option B \u2014 O(1) git calls)**:\\n1. Pull local cache: `backlog_list(section=\\\"P0\\\")` + `backlog_list(section=\\\"P1\\\")`\\n2. For each item, extract target file paths from Impact Radius section (or plan verification_steps)\\n3. Build union of all target paths across all items\\n4. Run one `git ls-files` command against the union \u2192 classify each path as present/absent\\n5. Per-item: map absent paths \u2192 NOT_APPLICABLE; then run `git log --after=\\\"{groomed_date}\\\" -- {present_paths}` per item to detect STALE; keyword grep for SUPERSEDED\\n6. Write triage report\\n\\n**Output**: `.tmp/scratch/reports/YYYYMMDD-stale-scan.md`\\nSections: NOT_APPLICABLE | SUPERSEDED | STALE | VALID | UNCLASSIFIABLE\\nEach entry: `#N title \u2014 evidence (file missing / commit SHA)`\\nCount summary at top.\\n\\n**Invocation**: `/dh:scan-stale-backlog` (all P0+P1), `--section P1`, `--since YYYY-MM-DD`\\nRead-only \u2014 never modifies items. Produces a report for human review + optional follow-up.\\n\\n**Acceptance criteria**:\\n- [ ] Runs to completion on all 237 open P0+P1 items\\n- [ ] NOT_APPLICABLE correctly flags items whose Impact Radius files are absent\\n- [ ] STALE correctly flags items with functional commits after groom date\\n- [ ] UNCLASSIFIABLE rate below 30% (items with no extractable file paths)\\n- [ ] Single git ls-files call for existence check (not one per item)\\n- [ ] Report includes count summary and per-item evidence\\n\\n**Depends on**: fix backlog_view groom date bug; improves significantly after #964 lands\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | Algorithm specified | AVAILABLE | Issue description: Option B \u2014 O(1) git calls, 6-step procedure |\\n| 2 | Output format specified | AVAILABLE | Issue description: sections, per-entry format, count summary |\\n| 3 | Invocation flags specified | AVAILABLE | Issue description: `--section`, `--since` |\\n| 4 | Groom date source | DERIVABLE \u2014 `backlog_view` returns groomed date; fallback to item creation date if absent |\\n| 5 | Target file path extraction from Impact Radius section | DERIVABLE \u2014 parse Impact Radius section body for file paths using regex or marko AST |\\n| 6 | Dependency on backlog_view groom date bug (#964) | AVAILABLE \u2014 described as 'improves significantly' not 'requires'; initial version can use creation date as fallback |\\n| 7 | Skill structure (SKILL.md + optional scripts) | DERIVABLE \u2014 follows existing skill conventions |\\n\\nVerdict: READY \u2014 all conditions AVAILABLE or DERIVABLE. Fully specified feature.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **feat: /dh:scan-stale-backlog skill \u2014 batch triage of open p0/p1 items for staleness** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Staleness policy design session 2026-03-30 \u2014 scan-stale-scope research agent\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-30\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP2 Feature. New skill directory created. Zero risk to existing functionality \u2014 read-only tool. Significantly improves backlog hygiene for large backlogs (237+ items). Depends on no blocking external items.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Skill runs to completion on all open P0+P1 items\\n- [ ] `NOT_APPLICABLE` category correctly flags items whose Impact Radius target files are absent from the working tree\\n- [ ] `STALE` category correctly flags items with functional commits touching their target files after the item's groom date\\n- [ ] `SUPERSEDED` category detected via keyword grep in item body\\n- [ ] `UNCLASSIFIABLE` rate below 30% (items with no extractable file paths)\\n- [ ] Single `git ls-files` call for file existence check (not one per item) \u2014 O(1) git calls\\n- [ ] Report written to `.tmp/scratch/reports/YYYYMMDD-stale-scan.md`\\n- [ ] Report sections: `NOT_APPLICABLE | SUPERSEDED | STALE | VALID | UNCLASSIFIABLE` with count summary at top\\n- [ ] Each entry includes: `#N title \u2014 evidence (file missing / commit SHA)`\\n- [ ] Invocation supports: `/dh:scan-stale-backlog`, `--section P1`, `--since YYYY-MM-DD`\\n- [ ] Read-only \u2014 never modifies backlog items\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/scan-stale-backlog/SKILL.md` \u2014 new skill (to create)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/scan-stale-backlog/references/algorithm.md` \u2014 optional algorithm reference\\n- Uses: `backlog_list` MCP tool, `backlog_view` MCP tool, `git ls-files`, `git log --after`\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a developer managing a large backlog of 237+ open P0/P1 items, I need a `/dh:scan-stale-backlog` skill that batch-triages items for staleness so that I can identify irrelevant or superseded items without manually reviewing each one.\\n\",\"digest\":\"5d41d4119dd67f3eee50d1b09c7f3c23539c8e1810c31444654f058ceb58de68\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg53oA\"}"}